          "rooms": [
            {
              "desc": "A one-seat cab set high over wide tracks, the seat empty and its harness clipped back. Where a driver's hands would rest a teleoperation repeater blinks green, carrying the bridge's commands down the link and the rig's cameras back up it. Through the rear glass the A-frame of a recovery boom stands over a winch drum as wide as the hull, and a pair of ground spades are folded against the tail. An Occator Water & Propellant lease tag is riveted under the stores gauge. The air is thin and cold and smells of grease and hydraulic oil.",
              "details": {
                "hitch box": "The wrecker's coupling controls: a winch, the spades and the boom on one panel. The plate reads RATED THREE TIMES OWN MASS, LADEN CASUALTY.",
                "repeater": "A sealed box with a green link light and a red one. Green means the bridge has the rig; red means nobody does, and the rig sits still until somebody does.",
                "seat": "Empty, its harness clipped back. A stencil on the headrest says CREW SEAT; rigs like this one are driven from the bridge.",
                "spades": "Two folded steel blades on rams at the tail. Dug into the regolith they hold the wrecker still while the winch takes a casualty's weight.",
                "stores gauge": "Tonnes and cubic metres in the tool locker against its two limits, 1 t and 2 m3."
              },
              "id": "cab",
              "kind": "walkable",
              "name": "Cab",
              "short_desc": "One empty seat high over wide tracks, a repeater blinking where the hands would go, a recovery boom through the rear glass."
            },
            {
              "desc": "A tool locker under the boom: chain, shackles, snatch blocks and cutting gear. Not a place anyone walks.",
              "id": "stores",
              "kind": "store",
              "name": "Stores"
            }
          ],
